From 2f7725cac31e891e20da9ac59380b0e22ed46784 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 14:39:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0194 -- a GUI that was not composited this
 frame loses its skip record

Fixes a stale-pixel defect in ags 0191, found by the standing present gate (ags 0193's DOSBox-X matrix): bench16 gui at
640x480x16 centred 1x read 480 of 1038 presents stale, 7,559 px each, the menu's rect.

The defect. ags 0191 skips a GUI's invalidation when its picture is provably the one already on screen: the real
pre-clear changed flags are clear AND its X/Y/W/H/transparency/z-order equal what its last composite was drawn from.
That record stayed valid while the GUI was HIDDEN. GUIMain::SetVisible marks nothing and a hidden GUI's texture stays
clean, so a re-shown GUI had no changed flag and identical properties: it passed SameAs(), its invalidation was skipped,
and the menu was composited into RAM but never pushed. 0191's hide side was right (guiskip hidden=25 for 25 hides); the
show was the miss.

The fix, one mechanism. draw_gui_and_overlays() notes which GUIs it composited this frame; any GUI it did not -- hidden,
fully transparent, or the UI layer not drawn at all -- has its record invalidated, so a re-show is treated as new and
marked normally. An unchanged, still-visible GUI is composited every frame, keeps its record, and still skips: stage 1's
win is intact by construction.

Why 0191's gate missed it, from counters (PLAN.md): at 2x the narrowing rejects every present (narrow=0 full=1500), so
a full push masks any narrowing bug; at the 8-bit alias rung the unchanged-frame path decided which ticks present (52 of
1041) and those were clean, while DOSAGS_PRESENT_NO_SKIP=1 on the same rung reads 480 of 1041 stale; only the 16-bit
centred-1x rung presents every tick with narrowing on the path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017rABavUPepUfapaKZYKPvD
---
 Engine/ac/draw.cpp | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Engine/ac/draw.cpp b/Engine/ac/draw.cpp
index 0875b9763..99fd271a2 100644
--- a/Engine/ac/draw.cpp
+++ b/Engine/ac/draw.cpp
@@ -437,6 +437,7 @@ struct DosPortGuiPrev
     }
 };
 static DosPortGuiPrev dos_port_gui_prev[64];
+static bool dos_port_gui_drawn[64];   // patch 0194: composited this frame
 long dos_port_gui_skip_tally[64] = {0};   // invalidations actually suppressed, per GUI
 long dos_port_gui_flush_n = 0;            // old rects invalidated ahead of the restore
 long dos_port_gui_flush_late_n = 0;       // ... found only when the GUI was drawn, a frame late
@@ -2753,6 +2754,9 @@ void draw_gui_and_overlays()
         gfxDriver->AddRenderEvent(kPluginEvt_PreGUIDraw, 0); // render stage
 
     clear_sprite_list();
+#ifdef __DJGPP__
+    for (int _i = 0; _i < 64; ++_i) dos_port_gui_drawn[_i] = false;   // patch 0194
+#endif
 
     // Add active overlays to the sprite list
     const auto &overs = get_overlays();
@@ -2966,6 +2970,7 @@ void draw_gui_and_overlays()
                         dos_port_gui_flush_late_n++;
                     }
                     _p.Record(gui, gui.GetX(), gui.GetY(), gui_ddb->GetWidth(), gui_ddb->GetHeight());
+                    dos_port_gui_drawn[index] = true;   // patch 0194
                     _p.unmarked = _skip;
                     if (_skip) dos_port_gui_skip_tally[index]++;
                 }
@@ -2978,6 +2983,17 @@ void draw_gui_and_overlays()
         }
     }
 
+#ifdef __DJGPP__
+    // DOS-PORT patch 0194: a GUI that was NOT composited this frame -- hidden, fully transparent, or
+    // the UI layer not drawn at all -- no longer has a composite that is "already on screen", so its
+    // skip record must not survive to qualify a later re-show as "the same picture as last frame".
+    // ags 0191 kept the record valid while the GUI was hidden: SetVisible marks nothing and the texture
+    // stays clean, so the re-shown GUI passed SameAs() and its mark was skipped -- composited into RAM,
+    // never pushed (bench16 gui at centred 1x: 480 of 1038 presents stale).
+    for (int _i = 0; _i < 64; ++_i)
+        if (!dos_port_gui_drawn[_i]) dos_port_gui_prev[_i].valid = false;
+#endif
+
     // Move the resulting sprlist with guis and overlays to render
     draw_sprite_list();
     put_sprite_list_on_screen(false);
